  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The external finishing materials shall match those used in the construction of the existing building and/or areas of hard surfacing. \rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice. \r\rSUDS PRO FORMA    \rE 00\rE 01\rE 02\rE 03\rE 04\rE 05\rP 00\rP 01\rP 02\rP 03\rP 04\rP 05\rP 06\rP 07\rP 08\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 7 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, the development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved cycle parking details as set out in (drawings ref: P 01 and P 08).\r\rThe cycle parking shall be retained and maintained as such for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in accordance with Policy T6.1 of the London Plan (2021), the Council's adopted standards and London Cycling Design Standards Chapter 8.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, the development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved Refuse details as set out in (drawings ref: P 01, P02 and P 07). \r\rThe refuse shall be retained and maintained as such for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: In order to facilitate efficient, safe and clean removal of household refuse, the location and accessibility of refuse storage plus to maintain safety on the Highway.\r"
  ],
